# =============================================================================
# LARGE / REGENERABLE FILES ONLY -- everything else (all CSVs, all scripts,
# README, requirements.txt) is tracked normally, including everything under
# processed/. This is a deliberate change from ignoring processed/ wholesale --
# that blanket rule is what made processed/iphone_whistle_candidates.csv (the
# manually-confirmed y/n whistle labels) unrecoverable when local files were
# lost. Small structural/index files should never be at that kind of risk
# again; only the actual audio blobs and the model binary are worth excluding.
# =============================================================================

# Raw source audio -- see README for download/setup instructions
raw_data/**/*.wav
raw_data/**/*.m4a

# Augmented/generated audio living outside raw_data/
data/augmented_dataset/
data/**/*.wav
data/**/*.m4a

# Processed AUDIO CLIPS only (the actual .wav files under processed/clips/).
# This is the large, regenerable part -- get these from the shared Drive
# folder instead of regenerating, or rerun the extraction scripts (02-04c)
# against raw_data/ if Drive isn't available. Everything else under
# processed/ (whistle_index.csv, match_negative_index.csv,
# iphone_negative_index.csv, iphone_whistle_index.csv,
# synthetic_negative_index.csv, iphone_whistle_candidates.csv,
# calibration_sample.csv, features.csv, test_set.csv) is NOT ignored --
# those are small and tracked normally.
processed/clips/**/*.wav

# Trained model binary -- large, and fully reproducible from
# processed/features.csv + 06_train_model.py's fixed random_state=42.
# Rerun 06 to regenerate, or grab from Drive.
models/*.pkl

# Python
whistle_env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db